# In-page navigation

Keep tabs and filters in one page when they share state; use route aliases instead of stub
pages that remount it. Preserve query parameters and the custom scroller's position.

Existing history-backed profile tabs bypass Vue Router alias deduplication. Their query
state must read `location.search`, write with `history.replaceState`, and react to `popstate`.
Inspect `useUrlFeedFilters({ historyBacked: true })` before extending that path; do not
introduce history-driven navigation where normal router navigation already preserves state.
